-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",347,{
[11073]="700173B8\n1\tDefeat Skûm\030Defeat Urauth\tSkûm and Urauth were last seen near the Forgotten Treasury, south and south-east of the Deep Descent in Moria. Hafberg told you of the twin trolls, Skûm and Urauth, alike in every way, and how they terrorize the dwarves in the area. You were asked to defeat them should you find yourself facing them.\n2\tReturn to Hafberg at the Deep Descent\tHafberg is at the Deep Descent, north and north-west of the Forgotten Treasury. After a long and difficult battle, you defeated the twin trolls to avenge the dwarves who fell to their cruelty.\n",
[11074]="70017514\n1\tReturn the carapace to Eilíefr at the Twenty-first Hall\030Collect Brúmbereth's Carapace\tBrúmbereth grows strong and raises many spawn among the corpses of Orcs in Skûmfil, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall where Elíefr stands. Elíefr has challenged you to defeat Brúmbereth in Skûmfil as proof of your worth as a warrior. Few are wilful enough to withstand the reek of that horrific place.\n",
[11075]="70017515\n1\tReturn the fang to Eilíefr at the Twenty-first Hall\030Collect Grimreaver's Fang\tGrimreaver grows strong and leads many minions among the corpses of Orcs in Skûmfil, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall where Elíefr stands. Elíefr has challenged you to defeat Grimreaver in Skûmfil as proof of your worth as a warrior. Few are wilful enough to withstand the reek of that horrific place.\n",
[11076]="70017521\n1\tDefeat enemies in Skûmfil (total: 50)\tKergrim and gredbyg grow strong and wicked among the Orc-corpses of Skûmfil, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall. Geirr has challenged you to defeat many of the vile creatures that lurk in Skûmfil as proof of your worth as a warrior. Few are wilful enough to withstand the reek of that horrific place.\n2\tReturn to Geirr at the Twenty-first Hall\tGeirr awaits tidings at the Twenty-first Hall, north-west of Skûmfil. You have defeated many kergrim and gredbyg in vile Skûmfil, and should now return to show Geirr that you are indeed as valiant as rumours have described. He will be glad to learn that you have proven yourself against the vile threat in the halls of the corpses.\n",
[11077]="70017517\n1\tDefeat Hwandrin\tHwandrin and her brood ever belch unwholesome filth upon the corpse-ridden halls of Skûmfil, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall. Sigurd has challenged you to defeat Hwandrin in Skûmfil as proof of your worth as a warrior. Her threat is great, yet few are wilful enough to withstand the menace of such an old and malevolent being.\n2\tReturn to Sigurd at the Twenty-first Hall\tThe dwarf Sigurd stands at the Twenty-first Hall, north-west of Skûmfil. You have defeated Hwandin at last; Sigurd is waiting to hear of your foray. You should return to him and illuminate all that happened in your battle against the Spider-queen.\n",
[11078]="70027F58\n1\tThe villagers can be found around the town of Lhan Tarren. You did not know many of these people personally, but they should be laid to rest below the earth all the same.\t\n2\tBury Elder Riagán's body\030Bury Blodwen's body\tAlso among the dead in Lhan Tarren are Elder Riagán and Blodwen, two people that you considered friends in Trum Dreng. You should lay the Elder and Blodwen to rest.\n3\tReturn to Guto\tGuto is grieving at the head of Lhan Tarren. You should speak with Guto and offer him your deepest sympathies.\n",
[11079]="7000B103\n1\tTalk to Taskmaster Sharkúlob at Gramsfoot and complete a patrol through the Ettenmoors as a Troll (Cost: 500 Commendations)\tTaskmaster Sharkúlob is at Gramsfoot in the Ettenmoors. The trolls from Angmar, in an effort to speed the victory of Angmar's army, are willing to come to the Ettenmoors to fight the Free Peoplea in exchange for your services in the North. You should speak with Taskmaster Sharkúlob.\n2\tTalk to Taskmaster Sharkúlob at Gramsfoot\tTalk to Taskmaster Sharkúlob at Gramsfoot in the Ettenmoors. You took the place of a troll in Angmar while it wrought destruction against the forces of the Free Peoples in the Ettenmoors. You should speak with Taskmaster Sharkúlob.\n",
[11080]="70019F86\n1\tDefeat Elves in Angmar (total: 10)\tYou have been instructed to defeat Elves in Angmar.\n",
[11081]="7000AC04\n1\tTalk to Taskmaster Sharkúlob at Gramsfoot and complete a patrol through the Ettenmoors as a Troll (Cost: 500 Commendations)\tTaskmaster Sharkúlob is at Gramsfoot in the Ettenmoors. The trolls from Angmar, in an effort to speed the victory of Angmar's army, are willing to come to the Ettenmoors to fight the Free Peoples in exchange for your services in the North. You should speak with Taskmaster Sharkúlob.\n2\tTalk to Taskmaster Sharkúlob at Gramsfoot\tTaskmaster Sharkúlob is at Gramsfoot in the Ettenmoors. You took the place of a troll in Angmar while it wrought destruction against the forces of the Free Peoples in the Ettenmoors.\n",
[11082]="700088A2\n1\tReturn to Taskmaster Izubuzri at the Isendeep Mine\030Collect Sun-touched tailfeathers (total: 10)\tEagles can be found throughout the Coldfells and in a small section of Arador's End to the south of the Isendeep Mine. Taskmaster Izubuzri wants you to return eagle feathers to him to prove that you have slaughtered a good number of the birds.\n",
[11083]="7003FFF2\n1\tDefeat slavers (total: 6)\tThe slavers must be defeated to secure the safety of those in Dol Amroth.\n",
[11084]="70040422\n1\tDefeat hounds in Lothgobel\tHounds can be found in a home in Lothgobel in central Lamedon. You should defeat hounds in Lothgobel.\n2\tDefeat war-hounds (total: 6)\tHounds can be found in a home in Lothgobel in central Lamedon. You should defeat hounds in Lothgobel.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the vicious war-hounds of the Corsairs in Lothgobel.\n",
[11085]="7005507A\n1\tFree enslaved Stout-axes in Bâr Maenath\tBâr Maenath can be found in the western reaches of the Circle of Death. You have encountered a number of enslaved Stout-axes in Bâr Maenath and should free them.\n2\tBâr Maenath can be found in the western reaches of the Circle of Death. You have encountered a number of enslaved Stout-axes in Bâr Maenath and should free them.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou have freed many of the enslaved Stout-axes in Bâr Maenath.\n",
[11086]="70027F1F\n1\tTalk to Edhere in the Orc-mines\030Talk to Meriun in the Orc-mines\tThe leaders of the two groups of slaves are somewhere in the Orc-mines. Ondor asked you to find the leaders of the two groups of slaves and convince them to work together against the Orcs.\n2\tConvince Edhere to go along with Ondor's plan\030Convince Meriun to go along with Ondor's plan\tEdhere and Meriun, the leaders of the two groups of slaves, may be found in the Orc-mines. You should speak again with Edhere and Meriun and convince them to form an uneasy alliance.\n",
[11087]="7000ED85\n1\tTalk to Arre\tArre is at the camp of Kuru-leiri, in the northern reaches of the great western glacier. Launo has asked you to speak with Arre concerning the fell spirits he reported.\n2\tDefeat wights in Kibilzahar ([see journal]/10)\tKibilzahar lies upon the northern slope of the glacier, north-west from Kuru-leiri. Arre asked you to explore the ruins of Kibilzahar. Perhaps you may solve the mystery behind the appearance of the fell spirits.\n3\tDefeat wights in Kibilzahar (9/10)\tKibilzahar lies upon the northern slope of the glacier, north-west from Kuru-leiri. Arre asked you to explore the ruins of Kibilzahar. Perhaps you may solve the mystery behind the appearance of the fell spirits.\n4\tCollect a frozen amulet\tKibilzahar lies upon the northern slope of the glacier, North-west from Kuru-leiri. While exploring Kibilzahar you discovered that some of the wights wandering through its ruins were wearing strange amulets. You should retrieve one of these amulets for Arre.\n5\tBring the frozen amulet to Arre\tArre is in Kuru-leiri, south-east from Kibilzahar. You should bring the frozen amulet you found in Kibilzahar. Perhaps he will be able to tell you more about it.\n",
[11088]="70027207\n1\tAssist Kai in Barnavon\030Assist Lunwen in Barnavon\030Assist Lhur in Barnavon\030Assist Eres in Barnavon\tKai, Lhunwen, Lhur, and Eres can be found within Lower Barnavon. Gwilum has asked you to lend aid to some of the inhabitants of Barnavon.\n2\tTalk to Gwilum in Barnavon\tKai, Lunwen, Lhur, and Eres may be found within Lower Barnavon. Gwilum has asked you to lend aid to the Boar-clan dwelling in Lower Barnavon.\n",
[11089]="70041C7D\n1\tFree enslaved Gondorians from ships in Pelargir (total: 8)\tSlaves can be found on the Corsair ships moored by the West Seagate in Pelargir. These ships can be reached by using nearby rowing boats. Firiondur has asked you to rescue any slaves that still have not been found on the ships in the harbour of Pelargir.\n2\tTalk to Firiondur inside the lighthouse at Aerthir\tFiriondur can be found inside the lighthouse at Aerthir. You have rescued several enslaved Gondorians and should now report your success to Firiondur.\n",
[11090]="70071636\n1\tDefeat Ordâkhai in Wither-watch (total: 15)\030Defeat Ulóngha Bóro\tThe Ordâkhai have taken over the town of Wither-watch and now use it as a base of operations. You should defeat the Ordâkhai and their leader, Ulóngha Bóro, in Wither-watch.\n2\tTalk to Kûrmi\tYou have defeated the Ordâkhai at Wither-watch. You should return to Ahâba and talk to Kûrmi.\n",
[11091]="7005AF83\n1\tDefeat Dulkoth the Slicer\tDulkoth the Slicer lurks somewhere in the tunnels in the north-eastern corner of the Pit of Stonejaws.\n2\tTalk to Gráfar Splitstone\tGráfar Splitstone waits to hear of your encounter with Dulkoth the Slicer.\n",
[11092]="7005A619\n1\tSpeak with Thromur once more\tThromur can be found in Amdân. Talk to Thromur.\n2\tTalk to Strázhek\tStrázhek is in Amdân. Thromur has asked you to speak with Strázhek.\n3\tSpeak with Tébakh\tTébakh is in Amdân. Strázhek has asked you to speak with Tébakh.\n4\tSpeak with Zebena\tZebena is in Amdân. Tébakh has asked you to speak with Zebena.\n5\tTalk to Thromur\tThromur can be found in Amdân. Talk to Thromur.\n",
[11093]="70048C9D\n1\tDefeat slimy blood-slugs (total: 10)\tSlimy blood-slugs can be found in the wilds of Agarnaith. You should defeat slimy blood-slugs.\n2\tCompleted.\t\n",
[11094]="70065F7C\n1\tExamine the first pin\030Examine the second pin\030Examine the third pin\030Examine the fourth pin\030Examine the fifth pin\030Examine the sixth pin\030Examine the first rope bundle\030Examine the second rope bundle\030Examine the third rope bundle\tAnnúngil has asked you to inspect ropes and pins on the Rosigil. The Rosigil is moored in the Dol Amroth bay.\n2\tReturn to the wharf master\tYou should let wharf master Annúngil know that you have examined many pins and piles of rope on the Rosigil. The wharf master is on a dock in the Dol Amroth bay.\n",
[11095]="7002BCAC\n1\tTalk to the escaped Dunlending prisoner in Nan Curunír\tThe escaped Dunlending prisoner is at a camp of Ox-clan merchants outside of Isengard in Nan Curunír. Gwin asked you to speak with a Dunlending who escaped from the dungeons of Orthanc during your own flight from there with Baldgar, after the Falcon-clan's betrayal.\n",
[11096]="7002EA84\n1\tDefeat salamanders in the Seething Mire (total: 10)\tSalamanders can be found in plenty in their nest to the south of Langhold, the Seething Mire. You should defeat many salamanders at the Seething Mire.\n2\tReturn to Higbald\tHigbald can be found in Langhold in the northern Wold. You should speak with Higbald.\n",
[11097]="700431B9\n1\tDefeat Haradrim scouts near Minlos (total: 8)\tHaradrim scouts have been sighted near the beacon Minlos, which overlooks the river Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin. Lady Terenis has asked you to investigate the Haradrim presence near Minlos and defeat them.\n2\tTalk to a guard at Minlos\tGuards can be found at the beacon Minlos in eastern Upper Lebennin. You have defeated many Haradrim scouts and should report to a guard at Minlos.\n",
[11098]="70065DBC\n1\tDefeat Corsairs (total: 8)\030Defeat Sadúkh\tThe defender at Minlos beacon has asked you to defeat Corsairs at a camp west of the beacon, along the road. Follow the road west to find Sadúkh's camp.\n2\tTalk to the Minlos defender\tThe defender at Minlos beacon should know that the road west to Tumladen is safe from Sadúkh's Corsairs. The defender can be found at Minlos beacon to the east.\n",
[11099]="7002EFBC\n1\tLook across the river at Amon Lhaw\030Climb Amon Hen and stand at the Seat of Seeing\tThe Seat of Seeing is located atop Amon Hen, east of Parth Galen. Ramdir has asked you to climb Amon Hen, defeating Orcs as you go, and to stand at the Seat of Seeing and look across the river.\n2\tTalk to Ramdir\tRamdir is at Hestil's camp near Parth Galen. You have seen evidence of a large massing of Orcs on Amon Lhaw and should report it to Ramdir.\n",
[11100]="70026F09\n1\tTalk to Bain in the centre of Lhan Rhos\030Collect baby slug-meat (total: 3)\tSlugs reside east of town. Bain is at the centre of Lhan Ros, west of the slug bogs. Bain wants you to hunt baby slugs for their meat.\n",
[11101]="7006212D\n1\tCollect beech nuts around Wylvenclove (total: 8)\tCadi has asked you to collect beech nuts around Wylvenclove, north-west of Herne.\n2\tTalk to Cadi\tYou have collected a number of beech nuts for Cadi. She waits in Rendal's home in the south-west corner of Herne.\n3\tHarvest seeds from beech nuts (total: 4)\tYou should help Cadi harvest seeds from the beech nuts.\n4\tTalk to Cadi\tThe beech seeds have been harvested. You should talk to Cadi.\n",
[11102]="7002F991\n1\tDiscover the láthbear den\tThe láthbears reside in the valley and den to the east of Faldham. The láthbears must be approached as an unavoidable threat. Attacking the creatures directly may be the only method of dealing with such a twisted foe.\n2\tDefeat daunting láthbears (total: 5)\030Defeat hulking láthbears (total: 5)\tThe láthbears reside in a den in the valley east of Faldham. Strike against the láthbears while they are unaware of your interference and prevent them from amassing a large attacking force.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have dealt a severe blow to the láthbear sloth that had risen as threat to the east of Faldham.\n",
[11103]="7004D06F\n1\tConfront Burudâur\tYou should confront the leader of the excavation, who is located on a raft at the edge of Esgaroth-of-old.\n2\tInvestigate the strange pile on the raft\tYou should investigate the strange pile on one of the rafts in Esgaroth-of-old.\n3\tLook at the Bones of Smaug\tSmaug's bones are in the water, in Esgaroth-of-old. You should find a good vantage place to inspect Smaug's bones.\n4\tTalk to Thorlind\tYou should talk to Thorlind, who can be found just outside of Esgaroth-of-old.\n5\tTravel to Lake-town\tYou should travel to Lake-town, north of Esgaroth-of-old.\n6\tSearch for talk of Smaug's bones\tLake-town can be found in the Dale-lands. You should look for anyone in Lake-town who is concerned with Smaug's bones.\n7\tTalk to Skerri\tThe unruly crowd can be found in Lake-town. You should find out why someone in the unruly crowd spoke the name of Smaug.\n",
[11104]="7006B6A6\n1\tDefeat usan-kûni (total: 8)\tYou should slay some usan-kûni, the scorpions gathered in Nirikal, the south-western desert of Ambarûl.\n",
})
